//! `string=', `string-lessp' and `assoc-string' read a symbol's name as Lisp
//! does, also when its key escapes the name (`symkey': a U+FDD0, a raw byte,
//! a code above U+10FFFF), for interned and uninterned symbols alike
//! (romacs#306). Each case's expected value is what pinned GNU Emacs
//! (45b0f769) printed for the same form.
